UNIT spec_version_for
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY package
ANCHOR rederive@b15b56613f9d cli/features.mjs specVersionFor over the feature table of cli/capabilities.json — reproduce the code exactly, accidents included
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG spec_version_for(features: list[text]) -> text
ENVELOPE features is a list of text of any length (empty and duplicates included). A name is matched exactly as given:
  case, whitespace and look-alike characters are significant. Throws are IN scope as observations (R3).
DEPENDS-ON none
DESCRIPTION The SIR spec version a bundle's feature set requires: the latest version among the features' FEATURES "since"
  versions, never below the floor "0.2". Under-stamping is the hazard the function guards, so a name it does not know
  throws instead of being skipped.
BEHAVIOR
R1 The result starts at the floor "0.2".
R2 Each name of features, in list order, is looked up in TABLE FEATURES; a hit whose since is LATER than the current result
  (TABLE VERSION-ORDER) replaces it. So the result is the latest since over the hits, or "0.2" when there are none; order
  and duplicates do not change it.
R3 A name that is not a row of TABLE FEATURES -> throws: the empty text, a case variant (Vectors, RING), a name with
  extra whitespace, and the names of the host's built-in object members (constructor, toString, __proto__, hasOwnProperty)
  alike. The throw happens even when the list also holds known features.
TABLE FEATURES — cli/capabilities.json "features": the feature name and its since; the implemented and generable flags are NOT consulted
  vectors           | 0.2
  carried-data      | 0.3
  envelope          | 0.3
  trace-seam        | 0.3
  scheduler         | 0.4
  lifecycle         | 0.4
  par-interleaving  | 0.4
  ring              | 0.4
  lang-variant      | 0.5
  cross-lang-anchor | 0.5
TABLE VERSION-ORDER — the since values compared as dotted numeric versions, earliest first; the result is always one of these four texts exactly
  0.2 | earliest, the floor
  0.3 | later than 0.2
  0.4 | later than 0.3
  0.5 | latest
INVARIANT the result is one of 0.2, 0.3, 0.4, 0.5; adding a name to features never lowers it; the input list is never mutated.
ORACLE value -> oracles/spec_version_for.json  CANONICAL-SHA256 883d849be39f7e385d110d66cf7738af3febb6b9066e56fb51fc3bea1a2aedaf
OUT-OF-DOMAIN outside the SIG (not representable under list[text], so not in the oracle): an argument that is not a
  list throws; a list element that is not text throws as an unknown name (R3).
SCOPE IN: R1–R3 over ENVELOPE, with the FEATURES table as it stands at the anchored commit. OUT: the rest of
  cli/features.mjs (detectFeatures, languagesOf, the general version comparator beyond the four since values), the
  throw message text (not graded), and non-text list elements.
PROVENANCE rederive@b15b56613f9d (rederive, the trust kernel's own cli), cli/features.mjs specVersionFor and
  cli/capabilities.json features.*.since. Cold cut 2026-10-26 into the v0.5 contract register from the pinned authority.
  Round 2 (authority b15b56613f9d): names are looked up as own rows of the table, so the inherited-name acceptance rule
  of round 1 is gone; the argument must be a list; the table is unchanged.
